# Contributing to @project_NAME@

Thanks for helping out. Bug reports, ideas and pull requests are all welcome.

## Reporting bugs and asking for features

Open an [issue](https://github.com/@project_REPOSITORY@/issues/new/choose) and pick the bug report
or feature request form.

Do not report security problems in a public issue. [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md) explains how to report
them privately.

## Making a change

1. Fork the repository and create a branch from `main`.
2. Build and run the tests:

   ```bash
   cmake --preset debug
   cmake --build --preset debug
   ctest --preset debug
   ```

3. Add or update tests for what you change.
4. Update the documentation when behaviour, build options or the public API change.
5. Open a pull request against `main` and fill in the template.

## Commits

Conventional Commits: `<type>(optional-scope): <description>` with the types
`feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`,
`chore`, `revert`.

## Code of conduct

Everyone taking part follows the [code of conduct](CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md).
